content.thinking:
All agents use flat frames like starfall. The website's new protocol stricter. The user explicitly says "站点上报协议（ready/progress/event/gameOver）对接参考 starfall-bulwark." Since starfall also flat (and would not register progress/event), perhaps acceptance only inspects frame kinds. Yet requirement "桥接与上报协议工作正常" implies functional. We should improve all 5 games to also include compatible `data` and `event` fields, without breaking their tests. Because tests may assert exact frames or payload fields. We can modify report wrapper centrally to normalize any flat payload into app-compatible payload while retaining flat fields:
```
function report(kind, payload={}){
 let frame={kind,...payload};
 if (kind==='progress' && !frame.data) {
   frame.data = { score: frame.score, progress: frame.progress, lap: frame.lap, level: frame.level, ... };
 }
 if (kind==='event') {
   if (!frame.event) frame.event = frame.tag || 'event';
   if (!frame.data) frame.data = {...};
 }
 if (kind==='gameOver' && frame.progress !== undefined && typeof frame.progress !== 'object') {
   frame.progress = { value: frame.progress, ...? };
 }
 if (kind==='ready') { ... maybe separate ready message }
 ...
}
```
But site's parsePayload:
- progress: returns `{kind:'progress', data}` only if data object. Adding data enough.
- event: requires `raw.event` string. Add event field.
- gameOver: parse returns kind with score and progress only if progress is object. If we set progress to object, tests may expect numeric progress. Need preserve numeric under another field `progressValue`; but tests might look at frame.progress numeric. Instead don't modify flat `progress`; we can add a `data` object containing progress, but app's gameOver parse only uses `raw.progress` object, ignores `data`. Could set `progress: {value: numeric}` and also `progressValue: numeric`; tests checking `progress` numeric would fail. Better we can include both? Duplicate keys impossible. Alternative send a separate app-compatible payload via postMessage only, while reportTarget frames stay flat. The report wrapper can create `frame` as flat for tests and then when posting to parent, transform to app-compatible message. That's ideal:
```
const wirePayload = toWire(frame);
window.parent.postMessage({payload:wirePayload})
```
- For reportTarget, keep flat.
- For progress, wire = {kind:'progress', data:{score, progress, ...flat}}.
- For event, wire = {kind:'event', event: frame.event||frame.tag||'event', data:{...flat}}.
- For gameOver, wire = {kind:'gameOver', score, progress:{value:frame.progress, ...flat}}.
- For ready, wire? The app expects lightgame:ready? It doesn't listen for it. We can still send `lightgame:ready` message separately; but the site sends ready handshake to game. For compatibility keep `report('ready')` but wire payload ready is rejected. Could send `{source:'lightgame',type:'lightgame:ready',gameId, v:1}` additionally in the report wrapper when kind ready and parent.
- For complete wire {kind:'complete',score}.
- Tests G.setReportTarget only get flat frames, unaffected.
- This would make integration truly work. Do for all 5 games. Also maybe update DESIGN? Not necessary, but wave report mention.
- Need ensure not causing extra network/external; postMessage only.
